body:
The apg opencode integration targets opencode 2.x. Four surfaces move together so the installed suite, its agents, and the repo config agree on one opencode version:

1. the `opencode-suite/` tool plugin — every suite tool runs as an opencode 2.x plugin built on `@opencode/plugin`;
2. the distributed agent templates (`opencode-suite/agents/*.md`) — the frontmatter carries the opencode 2.x permission model, and the `agent-builder` template generates opencode 2.x agents and maintains the repo-root `opencode.json` model map in the opencode 2.x shape;
3. the `apg init` install surface (`rust.apg.install`) — the plugin installs into the opencode 2.x plugin discovery location under `~/.opencode/` with the opencode 2.x plugin dependency, and the apg-owned stale file set prunes the obsolete `tools/apg_*.ts` namespace;
4. the user docs (`README.md`, `AGENTS.md`) — the opencode 2.x dependency is stated.

The port is a plugin-implementation port plus a native-shape adoption of the config surfaces; opencode 2.x reads legacy V1 config, so a repo's pre-existing `.opencode/` files keep loading while the repo moves to the native shape (`requirements.constraint.opencode-v2-support-window`).

Acceptance criteria: each of the four surfaces carries the opencode 2.x shape; the spine resolves from this requirement through its domain nodes and solution components to the edited code; `apg_spec_lint` passes the structural checks.
